james-will-1.md:1: argue/readings: S5 is read 2 ways: james-will-1.logic.r2 has "past_facts_bagged → dispense_warrant_past" and "past_facts_bagged" and "substance_droppable_past"; james-will-1.logic.r2.2 and james-will-1.logic.r2.3 have "past_facts_bagged → dispense_warrant_past"; they differ when only "we have already securely bagged our past facts in a certain order" and "we can dispense with any further warrant for the order of the past facts" are true, which the second allows
james-will-1.md:1: argue/answered: S5: answered yes, which keeps james-will-1.logic.r2.2 and james-will-1.logic.r2.3, to: Suppose "we have already securely bagged our past facts in a certain order" and "we can dispense with any further warrant for the order of the past facts" are true and "substance may be dropped from our conception of the irrecoverably past" is false. Is S5, "Truly enough, if we have {81} already securely bagged our facts in a certain order, we can dispense with any further warrant for that order.", true then?
